From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 02:21:23 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: a scanned PDF's words, read by the room's own
 reader

SpatiLoupe's PDFs are shown by SpatiMesh's viewer now (the owner, 2026-11-27: "webview, chromium
tools"), and SpatiLoupe read the text in a PDF's pictures with hemera, the room's own reader (its
Live Text; the owner, 2026-11-19: "I want it can select text from images (also on image of pdf)").
Chromium's viewer gives a page that is only a picture the words read in it -- chosen, copied and
found as a page's own (searchify) -- through Chromium's OCR service, Google's Screen AI library,
which the room has not got. That service (screen_ai::mojom::ScreenAIAnnotator) is answered here by
hemera (chrome/browser/spatiand/ocr.cc, bound in BindScreenAIAnnotator): the page's picture as
PNG to its POST /v1/ocr, with the room's AI settings (apps/ai.json: hemera's address, the reading
model, the first and second languages and then auto, and nothing sent when "read text in pictures
by itself" is off), its lines and words with their outlines in Chromium's form; a reader still
starting (503) is asked again after the wait it says. The request is let out by the firewall under
its own annotation (spatiand_ocr, in rules.xml and annotations.xml). Only how many lines were read
is logged, never what.
